{
  "id": "1288",
  "slug": "remove-covered-intervals",
  "title": "Remove Covered Intervals",
  "category": "dsa",
  "subcategory": "sorting",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "tags": [
    "Array",
    "Sorting"
  ],
  "statement": "Given an array `intervals` where `intervals[i] = [l_(i), r_(i)]` represent the interval `[l_(i), r_(i))`, remove all intervals that are covered by another interval in the list.\n\nThe interval `[a, b)` is covered by the interval `[c, d)` if and only if `c <= a` and `b <= d`.\n\nReturn _the number of remaining intervals_.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: intervals = [[1,4],[3,6],[2,8]]\nOutput: 2\nExplanation: Interval [3,6] is covered by [2,8], therefore it is removed.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: intervals = [[1,4],[2,3]]\nOutput: 1\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n*   `1 <= intervals.length <= 1000`\n*   `intervals[i].length == 2`\n*   `0 <= l_(i) < r_(i) <= 10^(5)`\n*   All the given intervals are **unique**.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= intervals.length <= 1000",
    "intervals[i].length == 2",
    "0 <= li < ri <= 105",
    "All the given intervals are unique."
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "intervals = [[1,4],[3,6],[2,8]]",
      "output": "2",
      "explanation": "Interval [3,6] is covered by [2,8], therefore it is removed."
    },
    {
      "input": "intervals = [[1,4],[2,3]]",
      "output": "1",
      "explanation": null
    }
  ],
